  "id": "COMPOUND:7785 - PROTEIN:733",
  "verbalization": "Ivacaftor is implicated in the target relationship with P-glycoprotein 1 through two distinct pathways. In the first pathway, Ivacaftor directly targets Kallikrein 14, which in turn targets P-glycoprotein 1. This suggests a chain of molecular interactions where Ivacaftor influences the activity of a downstream enzyme, Kallikrein 14, which ultimately affects P-glycoprotein 1. In the second pathway, Ivacaftor targets EC-GI-10, which is then targeted by tafluprost and finally by P-glycoprotein 1. While the exact mechanism by which EC-GI-10 influences P-glycoprotein 1 remains unclear, the shared involvement of P-glycoprotein 1 in both pathways indicates a potential role in the overall pharmacological response to Ivacaftor. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of drug-target interactions and the importance of understanding the molecular mechanisms that link different targets.",
